<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    {{ template "site_seo" (dict "Title" "API Documentation · bitcoin++" "Description" "Build apps and integrations with the bitcoin++ public API and OAuth authorization server." "Path" "/developers/api" "Image" "/static/img/rebrand/breakthroughs.jpg") }}
    {{ template "rebrand_header" . }}
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico">
    <script src="/static/js/api-docs.js" defer></script>
  </head>
  <body class="btcpp-api-docs-page">
    {{ block "mainnav" . }} {{ end }}

    <main class="api-reference">
      <header class="api-reference__bar">
        <a class="api-reference__identity" href="/developers/api">
          <span>bitcoin++</span>
          <b>API reference</b>
          <em>v1</em>
        </a>
        <button class="api-reference__search-button" type="button" data-docs-search-open aria-haspopup="dialog">
          <span>Search documentation</span>
          <kbd>⌘ K</kbd>
        </button>
        <nav aria-label="Developer resources">
          <a href="/api/v1/openapi.json">OpenAPI</a>
          <a href="/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server">OAuth metadata</a>
        </nav>
      </header>

      <div class="api-reference__shell">
        <aside class="api-reference__sidebar">
          <nav aria-label="API sections">
            <div class="api-reference__nav-group">
              <p>Get started</p>
              <a href="#overview" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="Overview">Overview</a>
              <a href="#quick-start" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="Quick start">Quick start</a>
              <a href="#authentication" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="Authentication">Authentication</a>
              <a href="#oauth" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="OAuth and PKCE">OAuth + PKCE</a>
            </div>
            <div class="api-reference__nav-group">
              <p>Resources</p>
              <a href="#conferences" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="Conferences API">Conferences</a>
              <a href="#people" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="People API">People</a>
              <a href="#recordings" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="Recordings API">Recordings</a>
              <a href="#hackathons" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="Hackathons API">Hackathons</a>
              <a href="#account" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="Account and talks API">Account + talks</a>
            </div>
            <div class="api-reference__nav-group">
              <p>Platform</p>
              <a href="#scopes" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="API scopes">Scopes</a>
              <a href="#conventions" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="API conventions and errors">Conventions</a>
              <a href="#rate-limits" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="Rate limits">Rate limits</a>
            </div>
          </nav>
        </aside>

        <article class="api-reference__article">
          <section id="overview" class="api-reference__hero" data-docs-section>
            <p class="api-reference__kicker">§ Developer platform</p>
            <h1>Build on<br><span>bitcoin++.</span></h1>
            <p>Published event data is open to everyone. Account and administrative operations use narrowly scoped bearer tokens with live ownership and role checks.</p>
            <div class="api-reference__hero-links">
              <a href="/api/v1/openapi.json">Download OpenAPI JSON →</a>
              <a href="/api/v1/bootstrap">Explore API bootstrap →</a>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="quick-start" class="api-reference__section" data-docs-section>
            <p class="api-reference__kicker">01 / Start here</p>
            <h2>Quick start</h2>
            <p>The stable base URL is <code>https://btcpp.dev/api/v1</code>. Public reads need no credentials and return only data already published on the website.</p>
            <div class="api-reference__inline-code" data-copyable>
              <button type="button" data-copy-code>Copy</button>
              <pre><code>curl -H 'Accept: application/json' \
  https://btcpp.dev/api/v1/bootstrap</code></pre>
            </div>
            <div class="api-reference__callout"><strong>Canonical contract</strong><p>The <a href="/api/v1/openapi.json">OpenAPI 3.1 JSON document</a> contains complete schemas and response definitions.</p></div>
          </section>

          <section id="conferences" class="api-reference__section" data-docs-section>
            <p class="api-reference__kicker">02 / Public resources</p>
            <h2>Conferences</h2>
            <p>Discover published events, their configured days, public agenda, speakers, sponsors, and talks.</p>
            <div class="api-reference__endpoints">
              <button type="button" data-api-endpoint="conferences" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="GET /conferences — List published conferences"><span>GET</span><code>/conferences</code><small>List published conferences</small></button>
              <button type="button" data-api-endpoint="conference" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="GET /conferences/{tag} — Retrieve a conference"><span>GET</span><code>/conferences/{tag}</code><small>Retrieve a conference</small></button>
              <button type="button" data-api-endpoint="agenda" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="GET /conferences/{tag}/agenda — Public agenda"><span>GET</span><code>/conferences/{tag}/agenda</code><small>Public agenda</small></button>
              <button type="button" data-api-endpoint="speakers" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="GET /conferences/{tag}/speakers — Event speakers"><span>GET</span><code>/conferences/{tag}/speakers</code><small>Event speakers</small></button>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="people" class="api-reference__section" data-docs-section>
            <p class="api-reference__kicker">03 / Public resources</p>
            <h2>People</h2>
            <p>Public people records are holistic: profiles include published talks, conference appearances, and hackathon projects without exposing email addresses or private contact data.</p>
            <div class="api-reference__endpoints">
              <button type="button" data-api-endpoint="people" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="GET /people — List public people"><span>GET</span><code>/people</code><small>List public people</small></button>
              <button type="button" data-api-endpoint="person" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="GET /people/{person_id} — Retrieve a public profile"><span>GET</span><code>/people/{person_id}</code><small>Profile, talks, appearances, and projects</small></button>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="recordings" class="api-reference__section" data-docs-section>
            <p class="api-reference__kicker">04 / Public + admin</p>
            <h2>Recordings</h2>
            <p>Browse published recordings anonymously. Conference and global admins can update recording metadata, then start, heartbeat, and stop HLS broadcasts with a scoped token. Global-admin services can incrementally poll the broadcast-plan feed to reconcile recording sources, release times, and destinations.</p>
            <div class="api-reference__endpoints">
              <button type="button" data-api-endpoint="recordings" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="GET /recordings — List published recordings"><span>GET</span><code>/recordings</code><small>List published recordings</small></button>
              <button type="button" data-api-endpoint="candidates" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="GET recording candidates — Admin recording work queue"><span>GET</span><code>/conferences/{tag}/recording-candidates</code><small>Admin recording work queue</small></button>
              <button type="button" data-api-endpoint="broadcast-plans" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="GET recording broadcast plans — Incremental stream scheduler feed"><span>GET</span><code>/recording-broadcast-plans?updated_after=…</code><small>Poll changed stream schedules</small></button>
              <button type="button" data-api-endpoint="recording-update" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="PUT talk recording — Update recording metadata"><span class="is-put">PUT</span><code>/conferences/{tag}/talks/{talk_id}/recording</code><small>Update recording metadata</small></button>
              <button type="button" data-api-endpoint="broadcast-update" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="PUT recording broadcast — Start or stop live playback"><span class="is-put">PUT</span><code>/recordings/{recording_id}/broadcast</code><small>Start, heartbeat, or stop HLS playback</small></button>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="hackathons" class="api-reference__section" data-docs-section>
            <p class="api-reference__kicker">05 / Public resources</p>
            <h2>Hackathons</h2>
            <p>Browse public competitions, submitted projects, confirmed teammates, published awards, and finalized results. Draft and disqualified projects remain private.</p>
            <div class="api-reference__endpoints">
              <button type="button" data-api-endpoint="projects" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="GET hackathon projects — Browse public projects"><span>GET</span><code>/hackathons/{id}/projects</code><small>Browse public projects</small></button>
              <button type="button" data-api-endpoint="project" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="GET hackathon project — Retrieve a project and teammates"><span>GET</span><code>/hackathons/{id}/projects/{project_id}</code><small>Project and teammates</small></button>
              <button type="button" data-api-endpoint="results" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="GET hackathon results — Finalized judging results"><span>GET</span><code>/hackathons/{id}/results</code><small>Finalized judging results</small></button>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="authentication" class="api-reference__section" data-docs-section>
            <p class="api-reference__kicker">06 / Authentication</p>
            <h2>Bearer tokens</h2>
            <p>Protected endpoints accept a personal API token created in Account Settings or an OAuth access token. Credentials belong only in the HTTP <code>Authorization</code> header—never in URLs.</p>
            <div class="api-reference__inline-code" data-copyable>
              <button type="button" data-copy-code>Copy</button>
              <pre><code>curl -H 'Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN' \
  https://btcpp.dev/api/v1/me</code></pre>
            </div>
            <div class="api-reference__callout is-warning"><strong>Scopes are not roles</strong><p>Administrative calls require both the requested token scope and the account’s current conference or global-admin role.</p></div>
          </section>

          <section id="account" class="api-reference__section" data-docs-section>
            <p class="api-reference__kicker">07 / Protected resources</p>
            <h2>Account + talks</h2>
            <p>Applications can read and update the current person’s profile, list their talks, and edit shared talk content. Schedule placement remains restricted to event administrators.</p>
            <div class="api-reference__endpoints">
              <button type="button" data-api-endpoint="identity" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="GET /me/identity — Retrieve identity and current roles"><span>GET</span><code>/me/identity</code><small>Identity and current roles</small></button>
              <button type="button" data-api-endpoint="me" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="GET /me — Retrieve the current account"><span>GET</span><code>/me</code><small>Current account projection</small></button>
              <button type="button" data-api-endpoint="me-update" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="PATCH /me — Update the current profile"><span class="is-patch">PATCH</span><code>/me</code><small>Update public profile fields</small></button>
              <button type="button" data-api-endpoint="my-talks" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="GET /me/talks — List the current person's talks"><span>GET</span><code>/me/talks</code><small>Current person’s talks</small></button>
              <button type="button" data-api-endpoint="schedule" data-docs-search-item data-search-label="PUT talk schedule — Schedule an event talk"><span class="is-put">PUT</span><code>/conferences/{tag}/talks/{talk_id}/schedule</code><small>Admin-only atomic schedule update</small></button>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="scopes" class="api-reference__section" data-docs-section>
            <p class="api-reference__kicker">08 / Authorization</p>
            <h2>Scopes</h2>
            <div class="api-reference__scope-list">
              <div><code>identity:self:read</code><p>Read your account ID, display name, and current roles.</p></div>
              <div><code>profile:self:read</code><p>Read your private account projection.</p></div>
              <div><code>profile:self:write</code><p>Update your public profile fields.</p></div>
              <div><code>talks:read</code><p>Read talks associated with your account.</p></div>
              <div><code>talks:write</code><p>Edit talks you speak at.</p></div>
              <div><code>schedule:write</code><p>Schedule talks when you administer the event.</p></div>
              <div><code>recordings:write</code><p>Manage event recording metadata.</p></div>
              <div><code>offline_access</code><p>OAuth only: request a rotating refresh token.</p></div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="oauth" class="api-reference__section" data-docs-section>
            <p class="api-reference__kicker">09 / OAuth</p>
            <h2>Authorization code + PKCE</h2>
            <p>Native, browser, and server-backed applications use the authorization-code flow. S256 PKCE, an exact registered redirect URI, and <code>state</code> are required.</p>
            <div class="api-reference__facts">
              <div><small>Authorize</small><code>/oauth/authorize</code></div>
              <div><small>Exchange</small><code>/oauth/token</code></div>
              <div><small>Revoke</small><code>/oauth/revoke</code></div>
              <div><small>Discovery</small><code>/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server</code></div>
            </div>
            <p>Access tokens last one hour. Approved <code>offline_access</code> grants a rotating 30-day refresh token. Bitcoin++ currently provides OAuth authorization, not OpenID Connect; identify the signed-in person and inspect their current roles through <code>GET /api/v1/me/identity</code>.</p>
          </section>

          <section id="conventions" class="api-reference__section" data-docs-section>
            <p class="api-reference__kicker">10 / Protocol</p>
            <h2>Conventions + errors</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>JSON keys use <code>snake_case</code>; timestamps use RFC 3339.</li>
              <li>Growing collections accept <code>limit</code> (maximum 100) and an opaque <code>cursor</code>.</li>
              <li>Public GET responses use ETags and short-lived caching.</li>
              <li>Mutations reject unknown fields; schedule collisions return <code>409 schedule_conflict</code>.</li>
              <li>Errors include a stable code, human-readable message, and request ID.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="api-reference__inline-code" data-copyable>
              <button type="button" data-copy-code>Copy</button>
              <pre><code>{
  "error": {
    "code": "insufficient_scope",
    "message": "The token does not grant the required scope.",
    "request_id": "..."
  }
}</code></pre>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="rate-limits" class="api-reference__section" data-docs-section>
            <p class="api-reference__kicker">11 / Operations</p>
            <h2>Rate limits</h2>
            <p>Initial limits are 120 public reads per minute per IP, 600 authenticated reads per minute per token, 60 ordinary mutations per minute, and 10 recording writes per minute. A <code>429</code> response includes <code>Retry-After</code>.</p>
          </section>
        </article>

        <aside class="api-reference__examples" aria-label="Code example">
          <div class="api-example" data-api-example>
            <div class="api-example__header">
              <div>
                <span data-api-example-method>GET</span>
                <code data-api-example-path>/conferences</code>
              </div>
              <button type="button" data-copy-example>Copy</button>
            </div>
            <div class="api-example__tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Example language">
              <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-api-language="curl">cURL</button>
              <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-api-language="javascript">JavaScript</button>
            </div>
            <pre><code data-api-example-code>curl -H 'Accept: application/json' \
  https://btcpp.dev/api/v1/conferences</code></pre>
            <div class="api-example__response-title"><span>200</span> Example response</div>
            <pre class="api-example__response"><code data-api-example-response>{
  "data": [
    {
      "tag": "dev26",
      "description": "..."
    }
  ],
  "meta": {
    "request_id": "..."
  }
}</code></pre>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </main>

    <div class="api-search" data-docs-search hidden>
      <button class="api-search__backdrop" type="button" data-docs-search-close aria-label="Close search"></button>
      <section class="api-search__dialog" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="api-search-title">
        <h2 id="api-search-title">Search API documentation</h2>
        <label><span class="sr-only">Search</span><input type="search" placeholder="Try “recordings”, “OAuth”, or “schedule”" data-docs-search-input autocomplete="off"></label>
        <div class="api-search__results" data-docs-search-results></div>
        <p><kbd>Esc</kbd> to close <span>·</span> Select a result to jump</p>
      </section>
    </div>

    {{ block "footer" . }} {{ end }}
  </body>
</html>
